    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d553">

                <pb facs="0649" n="581" xml:id="pg581"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72111/4469½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-01-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">24 January, 1917</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: It is only too probable
                    that Gerard’s conjectures in this matter are well founded. I wonder if you have
                    come to any fixed conclusion in your own mind as to whether the recent practices
                    of the British in regard to the arming of their merchantmen force upon us an
                    alteration of our own position in that matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
